:: Convo El Guyh Del Avrion [PanelLeft Avrion] {"position":"1400,16500","size":"100,100"}
(text-colour:yellow)[Avrion: I thought I had wiped you off my heel. I told you the child wasn’t for sale. And now you’ve enlisted these petty fools in your schemes. I could tear you limb from limb. Or leave you tied up here by the ankles until time forgets you.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Guyh: We both know the inconvenience isn't worth it. All considering. And I offer more than convenience.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Of course you do.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[They disobey me. And I have caught them, meddling. I apologise. I wished to sell them, among other things for the child.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Quiet about the child. Nothing you can offer me will change my mind. And even if you did have something, I wouldn’t take it, to spite you. Filth.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[The time has passed. I understand. I am honoured to be worth spiting. Perhaps you lash out?]

(text-colour:yellow)[Lash out. I wish my words could lash at you. Flay you in tatters. You black tongues disgust me. Hiding behind each other. Tongues with no teeth, no taste. All you have is your words. So I will let you have them.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Very well. My slaves have escaped me. That’s on me. I will purchase them back.]

(text-colour:yellow)[They are mine now. I am claimant without appraisal… I might just crush them in front of you for your insolence.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Let me arrest your suspicion. I have not come here for the child. I only fancied it. I have come to do you a favour. Come all this way.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Your favours are poison. And somehow you'll try convince me I want poisoned.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Your throne calls to you.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Silence you wretch. You know nothing of thrones. The very word should burn your tongue.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[The Myred Halls are already falling. The Saint is winning. And you are here prying hobbled thessals from cracked vessals.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Careful, little tongue. You are bleeding in the wrong direction…Are you lost?]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Don’t concern yourself with where my tongue rests. Concern yourself with what it says.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Hmmm, you are addled aren’t you. Addled to suggest I deal with the Saint, that he’d deal with demon.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[He has. Mulch.]

(text-colour:yellow)[You lie.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[You know it to be true. Now you know that, you carry these slaves as a burden; not a means to and end, but an end to a means. Let me purchase them back. And you keep the child.]

(text-colour:yellow)[You come to me with warnings and expect gratitude? You crawl in my shadow and speak of thrones. Perhaps you have more teeth than I had thought. 

Fine. But at double the cost. And I know you carry gold. You keep your teeth.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Don’t forget who came to you, when you reclaim your throne.]

(text-colour:yellow)[Do not mistake this for gratitude.]

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[I would never insult you like that.]


