strong><br>Employee accidentally took home a company pen.<br><br>Pen returned the following morning.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> None.</div><div class="office-employee-warning">NOTICE: Personnel review found no unusual circumstances, unexplained phenomena, ancient obligations or immediate workplace hazards associated with this employee.</div></div></div><div class="office-computer-menu office-database-return">(link-goto:"RETURN TO EMPLOYEE DIRECTORY","Office Computer - Employee Profile")(link-goto:"RETURN TO TERMINAL","Office - Computer")</div></div><div class="office-computer-footer">OMEGA CORPORATION — PERSONNEL RECORD OMG-00003</div></div></div>


:: Employee Database - Jerry {"position":"9100,5500","size":"100,100"}
(set:$CurrentRoom to "Youroffice")<div class="office-computer-screen"><div class="office-computer-window"><div class="office-computer-header">OMEGA PERSONNEL DATABASE</div><div class="office-computer-body"><div class="office-employee-file"><div class="office-employee-file-heading"><div class="office-employee-file-name">JERRY</div><div class="office-employee-file-subtitle">EMPLOYEE FILE OMG-00002 — ACTIVE</div></div><div class="office-employee-photo-frame"><img class="office-employee-photo" src="https://i.ibb.co/67PzcSd9/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-21-50-00.png" alt="Jerry employee photograph"><div class="office-employee-photo-caption">CORPORATE IDENTIFICATION PHOTOGRAPH</div></div><div class="office-employee-file-content"><div class="office-employee-section-title">BASIC INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">FULL NAME</div><div class="office-employee-value">Jerry</div><div class="office-employee-label">AGE</div><div class="office-employee-value">Unknown — estimated to be older than recorded history</div><div class="office-employee-label">SPECIES / ETHNICITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Avatar of Decay and Slime</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEX</div><div class="office-employee-value">Not applicable</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEXUALITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Does not understand the question</div><div class="office-employee-label">RELATIONSHIP STATUS</div><div class="office-employee-value">Bound to The Rot Eternal</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPENDANTS</div><div class="office-employee-value">Millions — primarily fungal colonies</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYMENT INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">POSITION</div><div class="office-employee-value">Senior Organic Asset Preservation Consultant</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPARTMENT</div><div class="office-employee-value">Facilities Management</div><div class="office-employee-label">START DATE</div><div class="office-employee-value">Unknown — employee was present before construction of the current premises</div><div class="office-employee-label">CONTRACT TYPE</div><div class="office-employee-value">Permanent</div><div class="office-employee-label">LINE MANAGER</div><div class="office-employee-value">Office Manager</div><div class="office-employee-label">SALARY BAND</div><div class="office-employee-value">OMEGA BAND B</div><div class="office-employee-label">PERFORMANCE RATING</div><div class="office-employee-value"><span class="office-employee-rating">★★★★☆</span> — one star deducted following repeated mould growth in Kitchen B</div><div class="office-employee-label">ESTIMATED ANNUAL WORKLOAD COMPLETED</div><div class="office-employee-value">96%</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">REGISTERED SKILLS</div><div class="office-employee-skills"><span class="office-employee-skill">MOULD IDENTIFICATION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">ARCHIVAL RECORD RETENTION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">INTERDEPARTMENTAL MEDIATION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">HORTICULTURAL MAINTENANCE</span></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYEE SUMMARY</div><div class="office-employee-text">Jerry has been employed by Omega Corporation for an indeterminate period of time. Exact employment records prior to 1983 were lost following the Basement Archive Incident.<br><br>Despite occasionally delivering lengthy speeches regarding forgotten kingdoms, apocalyptic wars and “the inevitable return of the Green Sovereign,” Jerry consistently completes assigned duties to an acceptable standard.<br><br>Facilities Management has learned that statements such as “the western chamber has begun to sour beneath the gaze of the dying moon” generally indicate a minor damp problem.<br><br>Highly regarded by Facilities due to his extensive knowledge of indoor plant care.<br><br>Generally quiet, considerate and pleasant to work with.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH ASSESSMENT</div><div class="office-employee-text">Employee occasionally experiences existential episodes relating to the collapse of ancient civilisations and the gradual decomposition of all living matter.<br><br>No impact on productivity.<br><br>No known risk to colleagues provided standard handwashing procedures are observed after prolonged physical contact.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">REASONABLE WORKPLACE ADJUSTMENTS</div><div class="office-employee-text">One potted fern must be maintained at the employee’s workstation.<br><br>Access to natural light where reasonably practicable.<br><br>Do not interrupt employee while communing with unseen realms. Episodes usually last between five and ten minutes and are generally comparable to an ordinary rest break.<br><br>Where possible, avoid seating employee directly beside dehumidifiers, industrial fungicides or consecrated ground.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">MANAGEMENT NOTES</div><div class="office-employee-text">Very polite.<br><br>Please discourage Jerry from referring to office renovations as “the desecration of sacred ground.”<br><br>Employees are reminded that Jerry’s discussions concerning “the Ancient War Between Realms” should not be interpreted as workplace grievances.<br><br>Water indoor plants weekly. Jerry becomes visibly distressed otherwise.<br><br>Avatar status has not affected punctuality.<br><br>When Jerry states that “the walls have begun to perspire with the memory of the drowned,” contact Building Maintenance and check the ventilation system.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">DISCIPLINARY RECORD</div><div class="office-employee-text"><strong>12/04/20XX</strong><br>Employee declared the photocopier to be “a gateway through which the Black Orchard whispers.”<br><br>Maintenance confirmed paper jam.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> None.<br><br><strong>03/11/20XX</strong><br>Employee covered Meeting Room B in moss.<br><br>Employees reported improved air quality and a measurable reduction in workplace stress.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Verbal reminder. Moss retained pending Facilities review.</div><div class="office-employee-warning">NOTICE: Omega Corporation recognises Jerry’s status as an immortal manifestation of decay solely for payroll, accessibility and equal-opportunities purposes. This recognition does not imply corporate endorsement of The Rot Eternal.</div></div></div><div class="office-computer-menu office-database-return">(link-goto:"RETURN TO EMPLOYEE DIRECTORY","Office Computer - Employee Profile")(link-goto:"RETURN TO TERMINAL","Office - Computer")</div></div><div class="office-computer-footer">OMEGA CORPORATION — PERSONNEL RECORD OMG-00002</div></div></div>


:: Employee Database - Stanley {"position":"9100,5300","size":"100,100"}
(set:$CurrentRoom to "Youroffice")<div class="office-computer-screen"><div class="office-computer-window"><div class="office-computer-header">OMEGA PERSONNEL DATABASE</div><div class="office-computer-body"><div class="office-employee-file"><div class="office-employee-file-heading"><div class="office-employee-file-name">STANLEY</div><div class="office-employee-file-subtitle">EMPLOYEE FILE OMG-00004 — ACTIVE</div></div><div class="office-employee-photo-frame"><img class="office-employee-photo" src="https://i.ibb.co/svGZDms3/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-22-02-03.png" alt="Stanley employee photograph"><div class="office-employee-photo-caption">CORPORATE IDENTIFICATION PHOTOGRAPH</div></div><div class="office-employee-file-content"><div class="office-employee-section-title">BASIC INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">FULL NAME</div><div class="office-employee-value">Stanley</div><div class="office-employee-label">AGE</div><div class="office-employee-value">34</div><div class="office-employee-label">SPECIES / ETHNICITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Human</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEX</div><div class="office-employee-value">Male</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEXUALITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Heterosexual</div><div class="office-employee-label">RELATIONSHIP STATUS</div><div class="office-employee-value">Single</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPENDANTS</div><div class="office-employee-value">None declared</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYMENT INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">POSITION</div><div class="office-employee-value">Senior Break Room Logistics Coordinator</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPARTMENT</div><div class="office-employee-value">Facilities Support</div><div class="office-employee-label">START DATE</div><div class="office-employee-value">03/02/20XX</div><div class="office-employee-label">CONTRACT TYPE</div><div class="office-employee-value">Permanent</div><div class="office-employee-label">LINE MANAGER</div><div class="office-employee-value">Office Manager</div><div class="office-employee-label">SALARY BAND</div><div class="office-employee-value">OMEGA BAND D</div><div class="office-employee-label">PERFORMANCE RATING</div><div class="office-employee-value"><span class="office-employee-rating">★★☆☆☆</span></div><div class="office-employee-label">ESTIMATED ANNUAL WORKLOAD COMPLETED</div><div class="office-employee-value">63%</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">REGISTERED SKILLS</div><div class="office-employee-skills"><span class="office-employee-skill">TEA PREPARATION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">BOX LIFTING</span><span class="office-employee-skill">VENDING MACHINE OPERATION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">MORALE BOOSTING</span></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYEE SUMMARY</div><div class="office-employee-text">Stanley is a friendly and enthusiastic member of the Facilities Support team. He maintains a consistently positive attitude and is well-liked throughout the office.<br><br>While Stanley occasionally requires additional supervision when undertaking unfamiliar tasks, his willingness to assist colleagues and cheerful disposition make him a valued member of Omega Corporation.<br><br>Frequently volunteers to help, regardless of whether assistance is required.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">MANAGEMENT NOTES</div><div class="office-employee-text">Please avoid assigning Stanley more than one task at a time.<br><br>Has an unfortunate habit of fixing problems that do not exist.<br><br>Continue encouraging independent problem solving.<br><br>Popular with staff.<br><br>Biscuits allocated to the communal kitchen should be clearly labelled.<br><br>Despite repeated incidents, staff unanimously agree that Stanley is "trying his best."</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">DISCIPLINARY RECORD</div><div class="office-employee-text"><strong>18/04/20XX</strong><br>Employee became trapped inside the vending machine while attempting to retrieve a packet of crisps.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Health & Safety briefing.<br><br><strong>02/09/20XX</strong><br>Employee accidentally activated the fire alarm after attempting to make toast using the office laminator.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Informal verbal warning.<br><br><strong>11/01/20XX</strong><br>Employee submitted an annual leave request addressed to "The Queen."<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Annual leave approved.<br><br><strong>27/06/20XX</strong><br>Employee unintentionally locked the Office Manager in the stationery cupboard for approximately forty-five minutes.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> No further action. Office Manager accepted Stanley's apology and described the incident as "mostly my fault somehow."</div><div class="office-employee-warning">NOTICE: Although Stanley has been directly or indirectly responsible for fourteen separate Health & Safety reports, Employee Satisfaction surveys consistently identify him as the colleague staff would most like to have lunch with.</div></div></div><div class="office-computer-menu office-database-return">(link-goto:"RETURN TO EMPLOYEE DIRECTORY","Office Computer - Employee Profile")(link-goto:"RETURN TO TERMINAL","Office - Computer")</div></div><div class="office-computer-footer">OMEGA CORPORATION — PERSONNEL RECORD OMG-00004</div></div></div>


:: Employee Database - Vlad {"position":"9000,5600","size":"100,100"}
(set:$CurrentRoom to "Youroffice")<div class="office-computer-screen"><div class="office-computer-window"><div class="office-computer-header">OMEGA PERSONNEL DATABASE</div><div class="office-computer-body"><div class="office-employee-file"><div class="office-employee-file-heading"><div class="office-employee-file-name">VLAD</div><div class="office-employee-file-subtitle">EMPLOYEE FILE OMG-00005 — ACTIVE</div></div><div class="office-employee-photo-frame"><img class="office-employee-photo" src="https://i.ibb.co/TMj6grNX/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-22-06-05.png" alt="Vlad employee photograph"><div class="office-employee-photo-caption">CORPORATE IDENTIFICATION PHOTOGRAPH</div></div><div class="office-employee-file-content"><div class="office-employee-section-title">BASIC INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">FULL NAME</div><div class="office-employee-value">Vlad</div><div class="office-employee-label">AGE</div><div class="office-employee-value">41 ( Self-reported: 647 )</div><div class="office-employee-label">SPECIES / ETHNICITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Human</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEX</div><div class="office-employee-value">Male</div><div class="office-employee-label">SEXUALITY</div><div class="office-employee-value">Not disclosed</div><div class="office-employee-label">RELATIONSHIP STATUS</div><div class="office-employee-value">"It's complicated."</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPENDANTS</div><div class="office-employee-value">Several bats (unverified)</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYMENT INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-data-grid"><div class="office-employee-label">POSITION</div><div class="office-employee-value">Night Shift Accounts Manager</div><div class="office-employee-label">DEPARTMENT</div><div class="office-employee-value">Finance</div><div class="office-employee-label">START DATE</div><div class="office-employee-value">31/10/20XX</div><div class="office-employee-label">CONTRACT TYPE</div><div class="office-employee-value">Permanent</div><div class="office-employee-label">LINE MANAGER</div><div class="office-employee-value">Office Manager</div><div class="office-employee-label">SALARY BAND</div><div class="office-employee-value">OMEGA BAND C</div><div class="office-employee-label">PERFORMANCE RATING</div><div class="office-employee-value"><span class="office-employee-rating">★★★★☆</span></div><div class="office-employee-label">ESTIMATED ANNUAL WORKLOAD COMPLETED</div><div class="office-employee-value">98%</div></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">REGISTERED SKILLS</div><div class="office-employee-skills"><span class="office-employee-skill">FINANCIAL RECONCILIATION</span><span class="office-employee-skill">EXCEL MODELLING</span><span class="office-employee-skill">ARCHIVE MANAGEMENT</span><span class="office-employee-skill">NOCTURNAL SCHEDULING</span></div><div class="office-employee-section-title">EMPLOYEE SUMMARY</div><div class="office-employee-text">Vlad is a dependable member of the Finance department who has demonstrated consistently high standards of accuracy and professionalism.<br><br>Prefers working evenings and overnight shifts. Has repeatedly requested an office without windows due to a self-described "rare sunlight allergy."<br><br>Displays a strong interest in Eastern European history and gothic literature.<br><br>Frequently volunteers to cover overnight accounting reconciliations when other staff are unavailable.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">MEDICAL INFORMATION</div><div class="office-employee-text">Employee has requested blackout blinds, access to refrigerated Type O blood storage and exemption from garlic-containing meals at company social events.<br><br>Occupational Health has approved these adjustments as reasonable accommodations for the employee's documented "rare sunlight allergy."<br><br>No evidence has been presented to support the employee's repeated assertion that he is an immortal vampire.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">MANAGEMENT NOTES</div><div class="office-employee-text">Please refrain from bringing live bats into the workplace.<br><br>Employees are reminded that Vlad's references to being an immortal vampire lord are considered part of his personal aesthetic.<br><br>Continues to decline invitations to the company summer barbecue.<br><br>Kitchen staff have requested that he stop labelling tomato juice as "Type O."<br><br>Despite repeated rumours, there is no company policy regarding wooden stakes.</div><div class="office-employee-section-title">DISCIPLINARY RECORD</div><div class="office-employee-text"><strong>18/10/20XX</strong><br>Employee was discovered sleeping upside down in the archive room.<br><br>Employee explained this was "more comfortable."<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> None.<br><br><strong>09/02/20XX</strong><br>Employee informed a new starter that he was "born before the invention of electricity."<br><br>New starter believed him.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Reminder regarding workplace professionalism.<br><br><strong>26/06/20XX</strong><br>Employee submitted a request for additional annual leave to observe "the Feast of Saint Vladislav."<br><br>No such holiday could be verified.<br><br><strong>Action Taken:</strong> Annual leave approved.</div><div class="office-employee-warning">NOTICE: HR recognises Vlad as a human employee for all contractual, payroll and pension purposes, irrespective of any claims to eternal undeath.</div></div></div><div class="office-computer-menu office-database-return">(link-goto:"RETURN TO EMPLOYEE DIRECTORY","Office Computer - Employee Profile")(link-goto:"RETURN TO TERMINAL","Office - Computer")</div></div><div class="office-computer-footer">OMEGA CORPORATION — PERSONNEL RECORD OMG-00005</div></div></div>


:: Enemy Turn Logic {"position":"12700,0","size":"100,100"}
(set:$CurrentCardTurn to "enemy")

(set:_enemyMessage to "")

(set:$PoisonSide to "enemy")
(display:"Resolve Poison")
(set:_enemyMessage to _enemyMessage + $PoisonMessage)

(if:$GameOver)[
	(set:$CardGameMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		"You defeated the enemy!"
	)
]

(else:)[



<!-- =========================================================
     ENEMY GAINS AND REFILLS MANA
     ========================================================= -->

(set:$EnemyMaxMana to
	(min:
		10,
		$EnemyTurnsTaken + 1
	)
)

(set:$EnemyMana to
	$EnemyMaxMana
)

(set:_enemyMessage to
	"Enemy turn. The enemy has " +
	(str:$EnemyMana) +
	" Mana. "
)


<!-- =========================================================
     EXISTING ENEMY CREATURES BECOME READY

     This occurs before the enemy plays any new creatures.

     Therefore, only creatures already on the board at the
     beginning of the enemy turn become able to initiate combat.
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[

	(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "ready" to
			true
		)

		(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "canInitiateCombat" to
			true
		)

	]

]


<!-- =========================================================
     DRAW UNLESS THIS IS THE FIRST TURN OF THE MATCH
     ========================================================= -->

(if:$TotalTurnsTaken is 0)[

	(set:_enemyMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		"As the first player, the enemy skips its opening draw. "
	)

]


(else:)[

	(set:$DrawSide to
		"enemy"
	)

	(display:"Draw Card")

	(set:_enemyMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		$DrawMessage +
		" "
	)

]


<!-- =========================================================
     ENEMY MAY PLAY UP TO THREE CREATURES
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _attempt,...(range:1,3))[

	(set:_chosenLane to 0)


	<!-- FIND THE FIRST EMPTY ENEMY LANE -->

	(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[

		(if:_chosenLane is 0)[

			(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length is 0)[

				(set:_chosenLane to
					_lane
				)

			]

		]

	]


	<!-- FIND THE FIRST AFFORDABLE CREATURE -->

	(set:_chosenCardIndex to 0)


	(if:$EnemyHand's length > 0)[

		(for:each _handIndex,...(range:1,$EnemyHand's length))[

			(if:_chosenCardIndex is 0)[

				(set:_examinedCard to
					$EnemyHand's (_handIndex)
				)

				(if:
					(_examinedCard's "type") is "creature" and
					(_examinedCard's "cost") <= $EnemyMana
				)[

					(set:_chosenCardIndex to
						_handIndex
					)

				]

			]

		]

	]


	<!-- PLAY THE CHOSEN CREATURE -->

	(if:
		_chosenLane > 0 and
		_chosenCardIndex > 0
	)[

		(set:_chosenCard to
			$EnemyHand's (_chosenCardIndex)
		)

		(set:$EnemyMana to
			$EnemyMana -
			_chosenCard's "cost"
		)

		(set:_chosenCard's "hp" to
			_chosenCard's "maxHP"
		)


		<!-- =================================================
		     NEW CREATURES ENTER RESTING

		     They may retaliate if attacked, but they cannot
		     initiate combat during the turn they were played.
		     ================================================= -->

		(set:_chosenCard's "ready" to
			false
		)

		(set:_chosenCard's "canInitiateCombat" to
			false
		)

		(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane) to
			_chosenCard
		)


		<!-- GRUFFALLO USES THE ENEMY'S MISSING HEALTH WHEN PLAYED -->

		(if:_chosenCard's "definitionID" is "gruffallo")[
			(set:_enemyGruffalloValue to
				(max:
					1,
					$EnemyMaxHP - $EnemyHP
				)
			)

			(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)'s "baseDamage" to _enemyGruffalloValue)
			(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)'s "damage" to _enemyGruffalloValue)
			(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)'s "baseMaxHP" to _enemyGruffalloValue)
			(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)'s "maxHP" to _enemyGruffalloValue)
			(set:$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)'s "hp" to _enemyGruffalloValue)

			(set:_enemyMessage to
				_enemyMessage +
				"The enemy Gruffallo entered as a " +
				(str:_enemyGruffalloValue) +
				"/" +
				(str:_enemyGruffalloValue) +
				". "
			)
		]


		<!-- =================================================
		     REMOVE CARD FROM HAND
		     ================================================= -->

		(if:$EnemyHand's length is 1)[

			(set:$EnemyHand to
				(a:)
			)

		]


		(else-if:_chosenCardIndex is 1)[

			(set:$EnemyHand to
				(subarray:$EnemyHand,2,-1)
			)

		]


		(else-if:_chosenCardIndex is $EnemyHand's length)[

			(set:$EnemyHand to
				(subarray:$EnemyHand,1,-2)
			)

		]


		(else:)[

			(set:_cardsBefore to
				(subarray:
					$EnemyHand,
					1,
					_chosenCardIndex - 1
				)
			)

			(set:_cardsAfter to
				(subarray:
					$EnemyHand,
					_chosenCardIndex + 1,
					-1
				)
			)

			(set:$EnemyHand to
				_cardsBefore +
				_cardsAfter
			)

		]


		(set:_enemyMessage to
			_enemyMessage +
			"The enemy played " +
			_chosenCard's "name" +
			" in Lane " +
			(str:_chosenLane) +
			". "
		)


		<!-- =================================================
		     RESOLVE THE CREATURE'S BATTLECRY
		     ================================================= -->

		(set:$TriggerCard to
			$EnemyBoard's (_chosenLane)
		)

		(set:$TriggerSide to
			"enemy"
		)

		(set:$TriggerLane to
			_chosenLane
		)

		(set:$TriggerMessage to "")

		(display:"Resolve Battlecry")

		(set:_enemyMessage to
			_enemyMessage +
			$TriggerMessage
		)


		<!-- =================================================
		     RESOLVE ANY DEATHS CAUSED BY THE BATTLECRY
		     ================================================= -->

		(set:$DeathMessage to "")

		(display:"Resolve Dead Creatures")

		(set:_enemyMessage to
			_enemyMessage +
			$DeathMessage
		)

	]

]


<!-- =========================================================
     SIMULTANEOUS COMBAT STORAGE
     ========================================================= -->

(set:_playerAttackSnapshot to
	(a:0,0,0)
)

(set:_enemyAttackSnapshot to
	(a:0,0,0)
)

(set:_damageToPlayerCreatures to
	(a:0,0,0)
)

(set:_damageToEnemyCreatures to
	(a:0,0,0)
)

(set:_damageToPlayerHero to 0)
(set:_damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats to 0)

(set:_poisonToPlayerCreatures to (a:0,0,0))
(set:_poisonToEnemyCreatures to (a:0,0,0))
(set:_poisonToPlayerHero to 0)

(set:_enemyInitiatedCombat to false)


<!-- =========================================================
     PHASE 1: SNAPSHOT ALL CURRENT ATTACK VALUES

     Food has its Attack calculated because it may retaliate.
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[

	<!-- PLAYER CREATURE ATTACK -->

	(if:(datanames:$PlayerBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:$AttackCard to
			$PlayerBoard's (_lane)
		)

		(set:$AttackSide to
			"player"
		)

		(display:"Calculate Creature Attack")

		(set:_playerAttackSnapshot's (_lane) to
			$CalculatedAttack
		)

	]


	<!-- ENEMY CREATURE ATTACK -->

	(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:$AttackCard to
			$EnemyBoard's (_lane)
		)

		(set:$AttackSide to
			"enemy"
		)

		(display:"Calculate Creature Attack")

		(set:_enemyAttackSnapshot's (_lane) to
			$CalculatedAttack
		)

	]

]


<!-- =========================================================
     PHASE 2: ASSIGN ALL COMBAT DAMAGE

     The eligibility checks are intentionally nested.

     This prevents Harlowe from misinterpreting multiple
     datamap possessives joined together using "and".
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[

	(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:_enemyCreature to
			$EnemyBoard's (_lane)
		)


		<!-- MUST HAVE EXISTED BEFORE THIS ENEMY TURN'S CARD PLAY -->

		(if:_enemyCreature's "canInitiateCombat")[


			<!-- MUST BE READY -->

			(if:_enemyCreature's "ready")[


				<!-- FOOD CANNOT INITIATE COMBAT -->

				(if:_enemyCreature's "tribe" is not "Food")[

					(set:_enemyInitiatedCombat to true)

					(set:_enemyDamage to
						_enemyAttackSnapshot's (_lane)
					)


					<!-- EMPTY PLAYER LANE -->

					(if:(datanames:$PlayerBoard's (_lane))'s length is 0)[

						(set:_damageToPlayerHero to
							_damageToPlayerHero +
							_enemyDamage
						)

						(if:
							_enemyCreature's "effect" is "self-damage-when-hitting-enemy-hero" and
							_enemyDamage > 0
						)[
							(set:_damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats to
								_damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats +
								_enemyDamage
							)
						]

						(if:
							_enemyCreature's "definitionID" is "leper" and
							_enemyDamage > 0
						)[
							(set:_poisonToPlayerHero to
								_poisonToPlayerHero + 1
							)
						]

						(set:_enemyMessage to
							_enemyMessage +
							_enemyCreature's "name" +
							" attacked through Lane " +
							(str:_lane) +
							" and dealt " +
							(str:_enemyDamage) +
							" damage to you. "
						)

					]


					<!-- OCCUPIED PLAYER LANE -->

					(else:)[

						(set:_playerCreature to
							$PlayerBoard's (_lane)
						)

						(set:_playerDamage to
							_playerAttackSnapshot's (_lane)
						)

						(set:_damageToPlayerCreatures's (_lane) to
							_damageToPlayerCreatures's (_lane) +
							_enemyDamage
						)

						(set:_damageToEnemyCreatures's (_lane) to
							_damageToEnemyCreatures's (_lane) +
							_playerDamage
						)

						(if:
							_enemyCreature's "definitionID" is "leper" and
							_enemyDamage > 0
						)[
							(set:_poisonToPlayerCreatures's (_lane) to
								_poisonToPlayerCreatures's (_lane) + 1
							)
						]

						(if:
							_playerCreature's "definitionID" is "leper" and
							_playerDamage > 0
						)[
							(set:_poisonToEnemyCreatures's (_lane) to
								_poisonToEnemyCreatures's (_lane) + 1
							)
						]

						(set:_enemyMessage to
							_enemyMessage +
							_enemyCreature's "name" +
							" and " +
							_playerCreature's "name" +
							" fought in Lane " +
							(str:_lane) +
							". " +
							_enemyCreature's "name" +
							" dealt " +
							(str:_enemyDamage) +
							" damage and " +
							_playerCreature's "name" +
							" dealt " +
							(str:_playerDamage) +
							" damage in return. "
						)

					]

				]

			]

		]

	]

]




<!-- =========================================================
     PHASE 3: APPLY ALL STORED DAMAGE

     Values are copied into temporary variables before changing
     the board cards. This avoids ambiguous chained datamap and
     array possessives in Harlowe calculations.
     ========================================================= -->

(set:$PlayerHP to
	(max:
		0,
		$PlayerHP - _damageToPlayerHero
	)
)

(set:$PlayerPoison to
	$PlayerPoison + _poisonToPlayerHero
)

(if:_damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats > 0)[
	(set:$EnemyHP to
		(max:
			0,
			$EnemyHP - _damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats
		)
	)
	(set:_enemyMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		"The enemy's attacking Goats also dealt " +
		(str:_damageToEnemyHeroFromGoats) +
		" damage to the enemy. "
	)
]


(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[

	<!-- =====================================================
	     APPLY DAMAGE TO THE PLAYER CREATURE
	     ===================================================== -->

	(if:(datanames:$PlayerBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:_playerCreatureBeingDamaged to
			$PlayerBoard's (_lane)
		)

		(set:_storedPlayerCreatureDamage to
			_damageToPlayerCreatures's (_lane)
		)

		(set:_playerCreatureCurrentHP to
			_playerCreatureBeingDamaged's "hp"
		)

		(set:_actualPlayerCreatureDamage to
			(min:
				(max:0,_storedPlayerCreatureDamage),
				(max:0,_playerCreatureCurrentHP)
			)
		)

		(set:_playerCreatureNewHP to
			_playerCreatureCurrentHP -
			_storedPlayerCreatureDamage
		)

		(set:$PlayerBoard's (_lane)'s "hp" to
			_playerCreatureNewHP
		)

		(set:$PlayerBoard's (_lane)'s "poison" to
			$PlayerBoard's (_lane)'s "poison" +
			_poisonToPlayerCreatures's (_lane)
		)

		(if:_actualPlayerCreatureDamage > 0)[

			(set:$DamagedCreatureSide to "player")
			(set:$DamagedCreatureLane to _lane)
			(set:$DamageActuallyDealt to
				_actualPlayerCreatureDamage
			)

			(display:"Creature Took Damage")

			(set:_enemyMessage to
				_enemyMessage +
				$DamageTriggerMessage
			)

		]

	]


	<!-- =====================================================
	     APPLY DAMAGE TO THE ENEMY CREATURE
	     ===================================================== -->

	(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[

		(set:_enemyCreatureBeingDamaged to
			$EnemyBoard's (_lane)
		)

		(set:_storedEnemyCreatureDamage to
			_damageToEnemyCreatures's (_lane)
		)

		(set:_enemyCreatureCurrentHP to
			_enemyCreatureBeingDamaged's "hp"
		)

		(set:_actualEnemyCreatureDamage to
			(min:
				(max:0,_storedEnemyCreatureDamage),
				(max:0,_enemyCreatureCurrentHP)
			)
		)

		(set:_enemyCreatureNewHP to
			_enemyCreatureCurrentHP -
			_storedEnemyCreatureDamage
		)

		(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "hp" to
			_enemyCreatureNewHP
		)

		(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "poison" to
			$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "poison" +
			_poisonToEnemyCreatures's (_lane)
		)

		(if:_actualEnemyCreatureDamage > 0)[

			(set:$DamagedCreatureSide to "enemy")
			(set:$DamagedCreatureLane to _lane)
			(set:$DamageActuallyDealt to
				_actualEnemyCreatureDamage
			)

			(display:"Creature Took Damage")

			(set:_enemyMessage to
				_enemyMessage +
				$DamageTriggerMessage
			)

		]

	]

]

<!-- =========================================================
     OLD BRIDGE DESTROYS THE CREATURE THAT KILLED IT
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[
	(if:(datanames:$PlayerBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[
		(set:_possibleBridge to $PlayerBoard's (_lane))
		(if:
			_possibleBridge's "definitionID" is "old-bridge" and
			_possibleBridge's "hp" <= 0 and
			_damageToPlayerCreatures's (_lane) > 0 and
			(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0
		)[
			(if:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "canInitiateCombat")[
				(if:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "ready")[
					(set:_bridgeKillerName to $EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "name")
					(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "hp" to 0)
					(set:_enemyMessage to
						_enemyMessage +
						"Old Bridge collapsed beneath the enemy " +
						_bridgeKillerName +
						", destroying it. "
					)
				]
			]
		]
	]
]


<!-- =========================================================
     TROLL AND GRUFFALLO HEAL AFTER COMBAT
     ========================================================= -->

(for:each _lane,...(range:1,3))[
	(if:(datanames:$PlayerBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[
		(set:_combatHealer to $PlayerBoard's (_lane))
		(if:
			_combatHealer's "hp" > 0 and
			(
				_combatHealer's "definitionID" is "troll" or
				_combatHealer's "definitionID" is "gruffallo"
			)
		)[
			(if:_combatHealer's "hp" < _combatHealer's "maxHP")[
				(set:$PlayerBoard's (_lane)'s "hp" to
					_combatHealer's "maxHP"
				)
				(set:_enemyMessage to
					_enemyMessage +
					_combatHealer's "name" +
					" healed to full Health after combat. "
				)
			]
		]
	]

	(if:(datanames:$EnemyBoard's (_lane))'s length > 0)[
		(set:_combatHealer to $EnemyBoard's (_lane))
		(if:
			_combatHealer's "hp" > 0 and
			(
				_combatHealer's "definitionID" is "troll" or
				_combatHealer's "definitionID" is "gruffallo"
			)
		)[
			(if:_combatHealer's "hp" < _combatHealer's "maxHP")[
				(set:$EnemyBoard's (_lane)'s "hp" to
					_combatHealer's "maxHP"
				)
				(set:_enemyMessage to
					_enemyMessage +
					"The enemy " +
					_combatHealer's "name" +
					" healed to full Health after combat. "
				)
			]
		]
	]
]


<!-- =========================================================
     PHASE 4: RESOLVE ALL COMBAT DEATHS
     ========================================================= -->

(set:$DeathMessage to "")

(display:"Resolve Dead Creatures")

(set:_enemyMessage to
	_enemyMessage +
	$DeathMessage
)


(if:not _enemyInitiatedCombat)[

	(set:_enemyMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		"None of the enemy's eligible non-Food creatures initiated combat. "
	)

]


<!-- =========================================================
     FINISH ENEMY TURN
     ========================================================= -->

(set:$EnemyTurnsTaken to
	$EnemyTurnsTaken + 1
)

(set:$TotalTurnsTaken to
	$TotalTurnsTaken + 1
)


(if:$PlayerHP <= 0)[

	(set:$PlayerHP to 0)
	(set:$GameOver to true)
	(set:$Winner to "enemy")
	(set:$CurrentCardTurn to "")

	(set:$CardGameMessage to
		_enemyMessage +
		"You were defeated!"
	)

]


(else:)[

	(set:$CardGameMessage to
		_enemyMessage
	)

	(display:"Start Player Card Turn")

]
]



:: EnemyTurn {"position":"7300,4700","size":"100,100"}
(set:$BattleInputLocked to true)
(set:$BattleTurn to "Enemy")
(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Action")
(set:$EnemyAttackHit to false)
(set:$EnemyDamage to 0)
(set:$BattlePopup to "")
(set:$BattlePopupType to "")
(rerun:?battleToolbarHook)
(rerun:?battlePopupHook)

(if:$EnemySkipNextTurn)[
	(set:$EnemySkipNextTurn to false)
	(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Skips Turn")
	(set:$BattleMessages to
		(a:
			$EnemyName + " looks at you quivering pathetically.",
			$EnemyName + " shakes its head at you.",
			"You're simply too pathetic to attack.",
			$EnemyName + " skips its turn!"
		)
	)
	(set:$BattleAdvanceAction to "FinishEnemyAttack")
	(display:"BattleShowMessages")
]
(else:)[
	(set:_enemyEffectiveSTR to
		$EnemySTR + $EnemyBattleSTRBonus
	)

	(set:_enemyEffectiveDEX to
		$EnemyDEX + $EnemyBattleDEXBonus
	)

	(set:_effectivePlayerDEF to
		$PlayerDEF + $PlayerBattleDEXPenalty
	)

	(if:_effectivePlayerDEF < 0)[
		(set:_effectivePlayerDEF to 0)
	]

	(if:$EnemyAI is "CaptainProductivity")[
		(set:$EnemyActionCount to $EnemyActionCount + 1)

		(set:_maximumFistDamage to
			(max:0,4 + _enemyEffectiveSTR)
		)

		(set:_fistCouldBeLethal to false)

		(if:_maximumFistDamage > 0 and $HP <= _maximumFistDamage)[
			(set:_fistCouldBeLethal to true)
		]

		(if:_fistCouldBeLethal)[
			(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction1)
			(set:$EnemyUseFistNext to false)
		]
		(else-if:$EnemyUseFistNext)[
			(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction1)
			(set:$EnemyUseFistNext to false)
		]
		(else:)[
			(set:_supportActionRoll to (random:1,2))

			(if:_supportActionRoll is 1)[
				(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction2)
			]
			(else:)[
				(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction3)
			]

			(set:$EnemyUseFistNext to true)
		]

		(if:$ChosenEnemyAction is $EnemyAction1)[
			(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Attack")

			(set:$EnemyAttackRoll to
				(random:1,20)
				+ _enemyEffectiveDEX
			)

			(if:$EnemyAttackRoll >= _effectivePlayerDEF)[
				(set:$EnemyAttackHit to true)

				(set:$EnemyDamage to
					(max:0,
						(random:1,4)
						+ _enemyEffectiveSTR
					)
				)

				(set:$BattleMessages to
					(a:
						$EnemyName
							+ " uses "
							+ $ChosenEnemyAction
							+ "!",

						$EnemyName
							+ " rolls "
							+ (str:$EnemyAttackRoll)
							+ " against your DEF "
							+ (str:_effectivePlayerDEF)
							+ ".",

						"HIT!",

						$EnemyName
							+ " deals "
							+ (str:$EnemyDamage)
							+ " damage."
					)
				)
			]
			(else:)[
				(set:$EnemyAttackHit to false)

				(set:$BattleMessages to
					(a:
						$EnemyName
							+ " uses "
							+ $ChosenEnemyAction
							+ "!",

						$EnemyName
							+ " rolls "
							+ (str:$EnemyAttackRoll)
							+ " against your DEF "
							+ (str:_effectivePlayerDEF)
							+ ".",

						"MISS!",

						$EnemyName + " misses."
					)
				)
			]
		]
		(else-if:$ChosenEnemyAction is $EnemyAction2)[
			(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Buff")

			(set:$EnemyBattleSTRBonus to
				$EnemyBattleSTRBonus + 1
			)

			(set:$EnemyBattleDEXBonus to
				$EnemyBattleDEXBonus + 1
			)

			(set:$EnemyDEF to
				$EnemyBaseDEF + $EnemyBattleDEXBonus
			)

			(set:$BattleMessages to
				(a:
					$EnemyName
						+ " uses "
						+ $ChosenEnemyAction
						+ "!",

					"His commitment to productivity intensifies.",

					$EnemyName
						+ " gains +1 STR and +1 DEX.",

					"His productivity bonuses have now stacked to +"
						+ (str:$EnemyBattleSTRBonus)
						+ " STR and +"
						+ (str:$EnemyBattleDEXBonus)
						+ " DEX.",

					"His DEF is now "
						+ (str:$EnemyDEF)
						+ "."
				)
			)
		]
		(else:)[
			(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Debuff")

			(set:$PlayerBattleSTRPenalty to
				$PlayerBattleSTRPenalty - 1
			)

			(set:$PlayerBattleDEXPenalty to
				$PlayerBattleDEXPenalty - 1
			)

			(set:_effectivePlayerDEF to
				$PlayerDEF + $PlayerBattleDEXPenalty
			)

			(if:_effectivePlayerDEF < 0)[
				(set:_effectivePlayerDEF to 0)
			]

			(set:$BattleMessages to
				(a:
					$EnemyName
						+ " uses "
						+ $ChosenEnemyAction
						+ "!",

					"Your productive output is forcibly reduced.",

					"You suffer -1 STR and -1 DEX for the rest of the battle.",

					"Your battle penalties have now stacked to "
						+ (str:$PlayerBattleSTRPenalty)
						+ " STR and "
						+ (str:$PlayerBattleDEXPenalty)
						+ " DEX.",

					"Your effective DEF is now "
						+ (str:_effectivePlayerDEF)
						+ "."
				)
			)
		]
	]
	(else:)[
		(set:$BattleStage to "Enemy Attack")

		(set:_actionRoll to (random:1,3))

		(if:_actionRoll is 1)[
			(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction1)
		]
		(else-if:_actionRoll is 2)[
			(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction2)
		]
		(else:)[
			(set:$ChosenEnemyAction to $EnemyAction3)
		]

		(set:$EnemyAttackRoll to
			(random:1,20)
			+ _enemyEffectiveDEX
		)

		(if:$EnemyAttackRoll >= _effectivePlayerDEF)[
			(set:$EnemyAttackHit to true)

			(set:$EnemyDamage to
				(max:0,
					(random:1,4)
					+ _enemyEffectiveSTR
				)
			)

			(set:$BattleMessages to
				(a:
					$EnemyName
						+ " uses "
						+ $ChosenEnemyAction
						+ "!",

					$EnemyName
						+ " rolls "
						+ (str:$EnemyAttackRoll)
						+ " against your DEF "
						+ (str:_effectivePlayerDEF)
						+ ".",

					"HIT!",

					$EnemyName
						+ " deals "
						+ (str:$EnemyDamage)
						+ " damage."
				)
			)
		]
		(else:)[
			(set:$EnemyAttackHit to false)

			(set:$BattleMessages to
				(a:
					$EnemyName
						+ " uses "
						+ $ChosenEnemyAction
						+ "!",

					$EnemyName
						+ " rolls "
						+ (str:$EnemyAttackRoll)
						+ " against your DEF "
						+ (str:_effectivePlayerDEF)
						+ ".",

					"MISS!",

					$EnemyName + " misses."
				)
			)
		]
	]

	(set:$BattleAdvanceAction to "FinishEnemyAttack")
	(display:"BattleShowMessages")
]


:: Enough questions. Time only goes forward [PanelLeft Door] {"position":"225,16475","size":"100,100"}
Guyh watches you.

Still.

The dark hides his face.

Then the light catches his teeth.

Grinning.

Or bared.

(text-colour:#7f7f7f)[Guyh: Time only goes forward.]

He matches your cadence.

Rey steps forward.

(text-colour:lime)[Rey: You can toy with our curiosity.]

He draws a steady breath.

(text-colour:lime)[But some answers are necessary.]

(text-colour:lime)[You said the castle was abandoned.]

[[...|abandoned]]


