:: Hold her hand and wait with her [PanelLeft Eggs] {"position":"300,5475","size":"100,100"}
You take her hand in yours.

Her fingers tighten suddenly, a weak desperate strength. Her breath falters, catching unevenly, and her body tenses as the pain moves through her. The fear in her eyes flickers- then steadies when she realises you are not letting go.

You stay with her.

The struggle slows. Her grip weakens. The light behind her eyes softens into something quieter, and finally slips away.

You hold on a moment longer, then gently close her eyes.

In the silence that follows, you notice a young woman standing behind you. She isn’t watching the dying woman so much as looking past her, as if following something leaving the world.

[[...|Untitled Passage3]]


