:: Keep running [PanelLeft] {"position":"575,11800","size":"100,100"}
Your lungs burn.

Your throat is thick with each breath.

The tunnel forks ahead.

Left- a shallow circle carved into the stone.

Right-three diagonal gouges cut deep.

You do not feel safe.

But you feel distance.

For now.

[[Diagonal|prediagonal]]

(if: $CIRCLE is false)[ [[Circle|precircle]] ]


:: Keep running, your legs have already made their decision [Eggs PanelLeft] {"position":"525,6025","size":"100,100"}
You both reach the embankment.

The castle vanishes behind the cliff.

You collapse to your knees.

A scream tears across the sand.

You turn.

The man has broken free. He stumbles through the shallow surge. His skin blistering, sloughing from his legs.

The tide is almost on him.

He forces himself upright and runs.

He barely clears the embankment as the wave crashes behind him, its spray hissing across his back.

He collapses beside you.

He writhes.

He does not have the strength to scream.

[[...|Breath2]]


