:: UwU {"position":"6900,2225","size":"100,100"}
(set: $i to 1)
(set: $t to "Clive’s nipples were harder than spring timber.

The ranch was cold. Too cold for a lonesome man.

The firewood crackled in the flames. He took off his jacket and held his nipples toward the fire, his broad chest gleaming with sweat and regret.

Outside, the wind dragged its claws across the wooden walls.

Then the wolf’s cry.

Long.

Low.

Lonely.

Clive froze.

Another howl answered it- closer this time.

The horses in the stable stamped nervously. Something heavy moved through the snow beyond the window.

Clive squinted into the darkness.
")

