:: diagonal [PanelLeft] {"position":"0,11500","size":"100,100"}
The path has narrowed- not by design.

The ceiling and walls have collapsed inward.

Stone and rusted fittings choke the floor.

A wrong step would flay the skin from your soles.

You move carefully.

[[...|diagonal2]]


:: diagonal2 [PanelLeft] {"position":"0,11600","size":"100,100"}
The tunnel collapses into a crawl space.

You drag yourself forward through dust and broken stone.

There is air here.

Faint- but moving.

It feels like hope.

Until the stone opens suddenly into a chamber.

[[...|diagonal3]]


:: diagonal3 [PanelLeft Pool] {"position":"0,11700","size":"100,100"}
The tunnel opens.

You rise into a chamber.

It slopes unnaturally downward.

As though sunk into the earth.

The path ahead is drowned in black water.

Still.

Bubbles rise and burst along the surface.

Each one releasing a stagnant breath.

Koemi holds the torch over the water.

(text-colour:lime)[Rey: All this way for a dead end.]

Koemi does not answer.

She watches her reflection tremble in the black.

(text-colour:#f1c9fe)[Koemi: Not a dead end.]

Rey exhales through his nose.

(text-colour:lime)[Rey: It is as dead an end as I’ve ever seen.]

Koemi lowers herself to sit at the water’s edge.

Rey turns to you.

(text-colour:lime)[We should turn back.]

[[We can't turn back now|diagonal4]]

[[It's too risky. We'll try our luck back the way we came]]


